    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "Hey, that is best neovim plugin i've found to animate scrolling (i'm using it standalone).\r\nWorks out-of-the-box, including to \"gg\" long file, without taking \"capturing\" nvim for minutes.\r\n\r\nBut it prevents me from scrolling the focused window with the mouse.\r\nMoving cursor just a bit if scrolling in really small steps.\r\nIf the window if not focused, it scrolls normally.\r\n\r\nI've tested that disabling \"scroll\" on config allow scroll with mouse, no other option (cursor, resize, etc) seems to interfere with that.\r\n\r\n\r\nTrying remap scrolls to movements, is kind of better than nothing, but not as responsive as the default scroll behavior (and can go strange on non-text buffers, like tree view and terminal):\r\n`3<C-e>` / `3<C-y>` - looks to be the spectated behavior of the scroll, but ends behaving the same as the plugin\r\n`j` / `k` - scrolls smoothly on normal mode, but may mess up with other, like registers\r\n\r\n---\r\n_sidenote:\r\nok, i know, [n]vim -> \"mouse less\"\r\nBut using a laptop, slid thumbs has sometimes a better ratio of speed/precision.\r\nSo not a habit i willing to drop just yet_",
