            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue.\r\n\r\n> But it prevents me from scrolling the focused window with the mouse.\r\n\r\nCould you, please, elaborate on this? Due to how Neovim works, every mouse wheel turn is a separate animation. So if you turn wheel to frequently, it tries to initiate animation every time which might contradict each other. Here is [the relevant part in help](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/doc/mini-animate.txt#L275).\r\n\r\n[Here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/177#issuecomment-1363816701) are some more insight from my point of view and [here](https://github.com/LazyVim/LazyVim/blob/main/lua/lazyvim/plugins/extras/ui/mini-animate.lua#L6) is how Folke resolves this. I personally set `vim.o.mousescroll  = 'ver:25,hor:6'` and prefer to turn mouse wheel one at a time.",
